      "id": "n1kxaiw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Economics"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Economics analyzes how society manages its scarce resources to satisfy unlimited human wants.",
        "Microeconomics focuses on individual decision-makers like households and firms, whereas Macroeconomics studies aggregate economic phenomena.",
        "The four essential factors of production are Land, Labour, Capital, and Entrepreneurship.",
        "Opportunity cost represents the value of the next best alternative foregone when making a choice.",
        "Basic economic activities encompass Production, Consumption, and Distribution."
      ],
      "id": "2oj6wwh"
    },
